# Edition 2, items batch 4: wondrous items, weighted toward the higher rarities.
# (name, category, rarity, attunement, text)
A = "Requires Attunement"
AS = "Requires Attunement by a Spellcaster"
W = "Wondrous Item"
ITEMS = [
# ================= COMMON =================
("Thimble of the Tailor's Ghost", W, "Common", None, "Set this thimble on a torn garment and speak the command word. Over the next 10 minutes, an unseen needle mends the tear neatly. The thimble can't mend magic items."),
("Wayside Kettle", W, "Common", None, "This small copper kettle boils up to a quart of water in 1 minute without a fire. The water can be poured hot or kept warm for up to 1 hour."),
("Cartographer's Ink Pot", W, "Common", None, "When you pour a drop of this ink onto paper, it spreads into an accurate floor plan of the room you stand in, with its doors and windows. The pot holds enough ink for 20 plans."),
("Gloves of Clean Hands", W, "Common", None, "While wearing these white gloves, your hands and the gloves never get dirty, and anything you wipe with them comes away clean."),
# ================= UNCOMMON =================
("Bracelets of the Bound Pair", W, "Uncommon", None, "These two copper bracelets come as a pair. While two creatures each wear one of them, each knows the direction and the rough distance to the other, as long as they are on the same plane of existence and within 1 mile of each other."),
("Collar of the Loyal Hound", W, "Uncommon", None, "A Beast that wears this collar understands simple commands in any language you speak, and it has Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the Charmed and Frightened conditions."),
("Pitons of the Sure Hold", W, "Uncommon", None, "This set of ten iron pitons sinks into rock, wood, or ice with a single tap, and each holds up to 1,000 pounds. On command, a piton you touch pulls free and falls into your hand."),
("Pack of the Long March", W, "Uncommon", A, "Objects you carry in this pack weigh half as much as normal. While you wear it, you can travel for 2 hours beyond the normal 8 hours each day before you risk Exhaustion from a forced march."),
("Plague Doctor's Mask", W, "Uncommon", A, "While wearing this beaked mask, you have Advantage on saving throws against diseases and against poisons that you inhale, and you can breathe normally in smoke and dust."),
("Tinker's Goggles", W, "Uncommon", A, "While wearing these goggles, you have Advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) and Wisdom (Perception) checks to find hidden mechanisms, traps, and secret doors, and you can read writing as small as a grain of sand."),
("Drum of the Marching Step", W, "Uncommon", None, "When you play this drum during travel, you and up to eight companions who can hear it have Advantage on saving throws against Exhaustion from a forced march, and a group that travels at a Normal pace covers 4 more miles each day."),
("Cloak of the Falling Leaf", W, "Uncommon", A, "While wearing this cloak, you can cast Feather Fall from it at will, targeting only yourself."),
("Bottle of Captured Wind", W, "Uncommon", None, "Once per dawn, you can unstopper this bottle as a Magic action to cast Gust of Wind (save DC 13) from it. The spell doesn't require Concentration and lasts 1 minute. Alternatively, you can let the wind fill a ship's sails, doubling the ship's speed for 8 hours."),
("Seeker's Compass", W, "Uncommon", None, "Once per dawn, you can name an object you have seen, or describe a kind of object, and turn the compass over in your hand to cast Locate Object from it. The needle points toward the object for the duration."),
# ================= RARE =================
("Boots of the Mountain Goat", W, "Rare", A, "While wearing these boots, you have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed, you ignore Difficult Terrain caused by rocks, scree, or ice, and you have Advantage on saving throws to avoid the Prone condition."),
("Gauntlets of the Siegebreaker", W, "Rare", A, "While wearing these gauntlets, your weapon attacks and Unarmed Strikes deal double damage to objects and structures. Once per dawn, you can cast Shatter (save DC 15) from the gauntlets, centered on a point you touch."),
("Chalk of the Hidden Door", W, "Rare", None, "Once per dawn, you can use this stick of white chalk to draw a door, up to 5 feet wide and 8 feet high, on a wall of wood, stone, or plaster that is no more than 1 foot thick. As a Magic action, you can open the drawn door, and it becomes a real opening through the wall for 10 minutes. Then the wall closes again, pushing any creature in the opening harmlessly to the nearest side."),
("Book of the Lost Hour", W, "Rare", None, "When you read aloud from this book during a Short Rest, each creature that listens to the whole reading regains Hit Points as if it had spent one of its Hit Dice, without spending it. A creature can benefit from the book only once per Long Rest."),
("Horn of the Shield Wall", W, "Rare", None, "Once per dawn, you can blow this horn as a Bonus Action. Each ally within 30 feet of you that can hear it gains a +2 bonus to AC and can't be pushed or knocked Prone until the start of your next turn."),
("Amulet of the Sworn Guardian", W, "Rare", A, "When you finish a Long Rest, you can name one creature you can see. Once per dawn, when that creature is targeted by an attack while it is within 30 feet of you, you can take a Reaction to teleport to an unoccupied space next to it. The attack roll then has Disadvantage."),
("Prism of Seven Lights", W, "Rare", A, "This crystal prism has 5 charges and regains 1d4 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can expend 1 charge to cast Color Spray from it, or 3 charges to cast Hypnotic Pattern (save DC 15) from it."),
("Pouch of Wardwood Seeds", W, "Rare", None, "This pouch holds 3 seeds and grows a new one each dawn, to a maximum of 3. As a Magic action, you can throw a seed at a point within 30 feet. A hedge of thorns fills a 10-foot Cube there for 1 hour. The hedge is Difficult Terrain, and a creature takes 2d4 Piercing damage for every 5 feet it moves through it."),
("Spyglass of the Far Watch", W, "Rare", None, "Objects viewed through this spyglass are magnified to ten times their size. Once per dawn, you can cast Clairvoyance from it, with the sensor appearing at a point you can see through the spyglass."),
("Torc of the Red Fury", W, "Rare", A, "While wearing this bronze torc, you have Advantage on Strength saving throws. While you are Bloodied, your melee weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 damage of the weapon's type."),
("Bell of the Last Rites", W, "Rare", None, "Once per dawn, you can ring this bell over a corpse to cast Speak with Dead from it. Once per dawn, you can also ring it as a Magic action: each Undead within 30 feet of you that can hear it makes a DC 15 Wisdom save or has the Frightened condition for 1 minute. A Frightened Undead repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."),
("Hourglass of Slowed Sand", W, "Rare", AS, "Once per dawn, you can turn this hourglass over as a Magic action to cast Slow (save DC 15) from it."),
# ================= VERY RARE =================
("Cloak of the Starless Night", W, "Very Rare", A, "While wearing this cloak, you have Darkvision with a range of 60 feet. While you are in Darkness and you move no more than half your Speed on your turn, you have the Invisible condition until the start of your next turn. The cloak doesn't work in Bright Light or Dim Light."),
("Circlet of the Clear Mind", W, "Very Rare", A, "While wearing this circlet, you have telepathy with a range of 120 feet and Advantage on Intelligence saving throws. You can cast Detect Thoughts (save DC 17) from it at will."),
("Bracers of the Mage Hunter", W, "Very Rare", A, "While wearing these bracers, you have Advantage on saving throws against spells. When you succeed on a saving throw against a spell cast by a creature within 30 feet of you, you can take a Reaction to teleport to an unoccupied space that you can see next to that creature. You can use this Reaction no more than once per turn."),
("Banner of the Last Stand", W, "Very Rare", None, "Once per dawn, you can plant this banner in the ground as a Magic action. For 1 minute, when an ally within 30 feet of the banner drops to 0 Hit Points but doesn't die outright, it drops to 1 Hit Point instead. Each creature can benefit from this only once each time the banner is planted. The effect ends early if the banner is moved."),
("Orb of the Waking Earth", W, "Very Rare", A, "While holding this orb of brown stone, you have Tremorsense with a range of 60 feet. Once per dawn, you can cast Wall of Stone (save DC 17) from it. The wall doesn't require Concentration, lasts 10 minutes, and can't become permanent."),
("Lens of the Hidden Truth", W, "Very Rare", A, "Once per dawn, you can look through this crystal lens as a Bonus Action to cast True Seeing on yourself from it."),
("Gloves of the Spellthief", W, "Very Rare", AS, "When a creature you can see within 60 feet of you casts a spell of level 1 to 5, you can take a Reaction to study it. Before you finish your next Long Rest, you can cast that spell once, using a spell slot you have and your spellcasting ability. You can hold only one stolen spell at a time, and you can use this property only once per dawn."),
("Drum of the Thundering Host", W, "Very Rare", None, "Once per dawn, you can beat this war drum as a Bonus Action. Until the end of your next turn, each ally within 60 feet of you that can hear it has a Speed 10 feet higher, has Advantage on attack rolls, and gains 10 Temporary Hit Points."),
("Tea Set of the Short Hour", W, "Very Rare", None, "Once per dawn, you can brew tea in this porcelain set as a Magic action. Up to six creatures who drink a cup within the next minute gain the benefits of a Short Rest, and they can spend Hit Dice as part of it."),
("Pelt of the Moonlit Pack", W, "Very Rare", A, "Once per dawn, as a Magic action, you can raise this grey pelt over your head and howl. You and up to four willing creatures within 30 feet of you transform into Dire Wolves, as if by the Polymorph spell. The effect lasts for up to 1 hour, as long as you keep Concentration (one Concentration for the whole group), and a creature can end it on itself as a Bonus Action."),
# ================= LEGENDARY =================
("Mirror of the Hidden Hall", W, "Legendary", None, "Once per dawn, you can hang this tall mirror on a wall and speak its command word to cast Magnificent Mansion. The mirror becomes the entrance to the mansion, and you can choose who can step through it."),
("Crown of the Unbroken Oath", W, "Legendary", A, "While wearing this crown, you have Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the Charmed condition. Once per dawn, you can cast Holy Aura from the crown."),
("Pocket Watch of the Stopped Moment", W, "Legendary", AS, "Once per 7 days, you can press the crown of this silver pocket watch to cast Time Stop from it."),
("Cloak of a Thousand Steps", W, "Legendary", A, "While wearing this cloak, you have the benefits of the Freedom of Movement spell. As a Bonus Action, you can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space that you can see. Once you use this property, you can't use it again until the start of your next turn."),
]
